{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791728994,"nonce":"clpsh9d6Fr0Tg05L73BAgayP0XM=","title":"z-index","message":"z-index is an integer or auto (router id 121, an owned-context id as order's 118 is). Siblings stack as CSS stacks a context's children: a negative z-index under the rest, the rest in tree order, then z-index 0 and sticky nodes in tree order, then positive ones, ties in tree order; the display list paints in that order and the hit test takes it in reverse, through one function, Tree::paint_order.\n\nTwo deliberate limits, to keep the other SDK's existing paint order: a node with no z-index keeps tree order, positioned or not (CSS would lift position: absolute over in-flow siblings); and each node stacks only among its own siblings, as if it began a stacking context, so a deeply nested z-index cannot rise over its ancestors' siblings. Say so on the wiki; revisit if either bites.","files":null}]}